CommitDate: Wed Oct 7 00:38:18 2026 -0500

    perf(asof): batch chunk reads via one cat-file --batch + whole-tree ls-tree
    
    GET /api/memories?as_of=... spent its prod-scale latency spawning one git
    child process per chunk (one ls-tree per partition + one git show per
    chunk — hundreds of execFileSync round-trips on a 245k-row namespace).
    
    readRowsAtRef now:
    - lists ALL chunk files with ONE git ls-tree -r over the whole ref
    - reads the manifest + every *.jsonl chunk through ONE
      git cat-file --batch process (spawnSync, in-order responses matched
      to requests by position; hits '<oid> blob <size>', misses '<req> missing')
    - readManifestAtRef gains an optional preloaded map so the hot path
      parses the manifest from the batch without a dedicated git call
    
    Semantics unchanged (dedup latest-per-id, tombstone exclusion,
    filter-before-dedup, timestamp DESC / id ASC, limit/offset last) and
    locked by a new PERF-011 test block: identical-results test against a
    per-chunk git-show reference reader on a multi-partition fixture with
    duplicate ids across chunks and tombstones, plus a <=3-git-process
    count assertion (was 2 + chunks).
    
    Measured on a 200-chunk / 20k-row fixture: per-chunk spawn 1588ms vs
    batched 54ms (~29x on the read fan-out).
    
    Addresses PERF-011.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
